        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "92e3f0cd-e38a-551d-a12f-62b19a9c0dcc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Pinocchio (1940 film), Home on the Range (2004 film), \"I've Got No Strings\", Snow White and the Seven Dwarfs (1937), The Adventures of Pinocchio\n- Companies: Walt Disney Productions, Walt Disney Feature Animation, Walt Disney Pictures\n- People: Carlo Collodi, Dickie Jones\n- Topics: animated films, Disney films, film production, songs\n\nFacts:\n- In 1940, Pinocchio was released as an American animated musical fantasy film produced by Walt Disney Productions.\n- Pinocchio was based on The Adventures of Pinocchio, an Italian children's novel by Carlo Collodi.\n- Pinocchio was Disney's second animated feature film and was made after the success of Snow White and the Seven Dwarfs in 1937.\n- \"I've Got No Strings,\" also known as \"I Got No Strings,\" is a song from Walt Disney's animated film Pinocchio sung by Dickie Jones as Pinocchio.\n- In 2004, Home on the Range was released as an American animated musical western comedy film produced by Walt Disney Feature Animation and released by Walt Disney Pictures.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
